+## Submission and Idempotency
+
+- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL retain the submitted payload with its visit ID, author ID, base revision ID, idempotency key, and server receipt time.
+- [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload and base_revision_id, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result with the existing revision ID without creating another stored submission.
+- [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission with a conflict error and leave the original submission unchanged.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When a submission's base_revision_id does not exist or refers to a different visit, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+
+## Revision and Conflict Detection
+
+- [ ] **REC-005**: When multiple submissions with the same visit ID arrive with the same base_revision_id, the system SHALL create multiple competing revisions with distinct revision IDs.
+- [ ] **REC-006**: When a visit has unresolved competing revisions, the system SHALL mark that visit as having unresolved review work.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a retrieval request includes a visit with unresolved competing revisions, the system SHALL return the has_unresolved_revisions flag as true and the metadata for all competing revisions (author, submission time, base_revision_id, submitted field payload).
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a retrieval request includes a visit with a single accepted or merged revision, the system SHALL return that revision's state as the current visit and the has_unresolved_revisions flag as false.
+
+## Resolution Operations
+
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a coordinator accepts a revision, the system SHALL mark that revision as the current state, record the coordinator's identity and resolution time, and clear the unresolved flag for that visit.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a coordinator merges revisions, the system SHALL store the merged fields as a new revision, record the merged revision as deriving from the multiple competing base revisions, record the coordinator's identity and resolution time, and clear the unresolved flag for that visit.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a coordinator requests clarification, the system SHALL store a clarification request note, keep the visit in unresolved status, and return the note to the field worker on their next sync.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: The system SHALL never delete an original submission or revision, even after a coordinator accepts, merges, or requests clarification. All history SHALL remain retrievable for audit.
+
+## Preservation of Submitted Edits
+
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions as distinct revisions.
